IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`

-- g9-tests-periods.l4: tests of the counting in g9-common.l4. Every expected value below was worked out from the text of the Law and the calendar BEFORE the module was run
-- (the day arithmetic is by hand: 14 days is two weeks; 2028, 2032 and 2036 are leap years; 2026 and 2027 are not). Each fork is tested on both sides of its threshold, under reading A
-- (the favoured interpretation) and under the other reading. The Schedule modules' own figures (3 months, 4 weeks) are tested in their own test modules.

`A` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`

§ `F9.1: at least 2 weeks before appointing`
-- appointment on 15 March 2026: reading A allows the notice up to 1 March (14 days before), reading B up to 28 February (14 clear days: 15 days before)
`B of F9.1` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.1 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of intention before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 15) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of intention before an appointment` `B of F9.1` (YMD 2026 3 15) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `B of F9.1` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 2 28) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `B of F9.1` (YMD 2026 2 28) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `B of F9.1` (YMD 2026 3 2) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
-- a notice on the day of the appointment is in time under neither reading
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of intention was presented in time before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
-- one week instead of two moves the day by seven
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of intention before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 15) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 8
-- the reading functions themselves
#ASSERT `F9.1 reading A: the latest day for a notice that must precede an event by that many weeks` (YMD 2026 3 15) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `F9.1 reading B: the latest day for a notice that leaves that many clear weeks before an event` (YMD 2026 3 15) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

§ `F9.14: before appointing, the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission`
`B of F9.14` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.14 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission to be sought` `A` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission to be sought` `B of F9.14` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 14) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` `B of F9.14` (YMD 2026 3 15) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` `B of F9.14` (YMD 2026 3 16) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 16) (YMD 2026 3 15)

§ `F9.2: a period of the appointment of not more than 6 years`
-- a term from 1 March 2026: reading A allows the end date 1 March 2032 (the 6th anniversary), reading B only 29 February 2032 (2032 is a leap year)
`B of F9.2` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.2 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest end date of a term of an appointment` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) 6 EQUALS YMD 2032 3 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest end date of a term of an appointment` `B of F9.2` (YMD 2026 3 1) 6 EQUALS YMD 2032 2 29
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) 6
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `B of F9.2` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1) 6
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 2 29) 6
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `B of F9.2` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 2 29) 6
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 2) 6
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a term of an appointment is not more than that many years` `B of F9.2` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 2) 6
-- a start on 29 February 2028: the 6th anniversary is 28 February 2034 (daydate `add years` clamps), the day before it 27 February
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest end date of a term of an appointment` `A` (YMD 2028 2 29) 6 EQUALS YMD 2034 2 28
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest end date of a term of an appointment` `B of F9.2` (YMD 2028 2 29) 6 EQUALS YMD 2034 2 27

§ `F9.3: resigning by giving not less than a number of months' notice`
-- notice given on 30 November 2026, three months: clamped 28 February 2027; rolled, 30 February is 2 March 2027
`B of F9.3` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as B`
`C of F9.3` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as C`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `A` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `B of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 2
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of resignation is for not less than that many months` `A` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 28) 3
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of resignation is for not less than that many months` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 28) 3
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of resignation is for not less than that many months` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 3 2) 3
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of resignation is for not less than that many months` `A` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 27) 3
-- where the office ends: when the notice runs out (A, C) or when it is given (B); a notice that is too short is no resignation
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` `A` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 28) 3 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 2 28)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` `B of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 28) 3 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 11 30)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 3 2) 3 EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 28) 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day the office ends by resignation` `A` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 2 27) 3 EQUALS NOTHING
-- one month (Schedule 2): a notice on 31 January 2026 clamps to 28 February and rolls to 3 March
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `A` (YMD 2026 1 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 1 31) 1 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 3
-- an ordinary date: all readings agree
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `A` (YMD 2026 5 15) 3 EQUALS YMD 2026 8 15
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the earliest day a notice of resignation can name` `C of F9.3` (YMD 2026 5 15) 3 EQUALS YMD 2026 8 15

§ `F9.4: absent for a period longer than a number of consecutive weeks`
-- 4 weeks is 28 days. Absent from 1 to 29 March 2026: 29 days counted, 28 elapsed.
`B of F9.4` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.4 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 29) 4
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 29) 4
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 28) 4
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 28) 4
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 30) 4
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 30) 4
-- 8 weeks is 56 days. 1 March to 25 April 2026 is 56 days counted (55 elapsed); to 26 April 57 (56 elapsed); to 27 April 58 (57 elapsed).
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 25) 8
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 26) 8
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 26) 8
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: an absence from duties was for a period longer than that many consecutive weeks` `B of F9.4` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 27) 8

§ `F9.5: not more than 2 weeks after terminating`
`B of F9.5` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.5 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of a termination` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a notice of a termination` `B of F9.5` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `B of F9.5` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15) 2
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `B of F9.5` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 14) 2
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 16) 2
-- a notice presented before the termination is not a notice that the Minister has terminated
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 2 28) 2
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a notice of a termination was presented in time` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) 2

§ `F9.6 and F9.11: completing 12 years of service`
-- Service periods. Continuous service from 1 March 2026: the 12th anniversary is 1 March 2038; 12 calendar years from 1 March 2026 are 4,383 days (leap days 29 Feb 2028, 2032 and 2036), 12 years of 365 days are 4,380.
`B of F9.6` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.6 is read as B`
`B of F9.11` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.11 is read as B`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
`no service before` MEANS EMPTY

`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2036-03-01` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2036 3 1), FALSE
`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2030-03-01` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2030 3 1), FALSE
`a spell from 2032-06-01 to 2036-06-01` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2032 6 1), (YMD 2036 6 1), FALSE
`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2038-03-01` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2038 3 1), FALSE
`a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2027-05-01 as a designated person` MEANS `Period of service under the Schedules` OF (YMD 2026 3 1), (YMD 2027 5 1), TRUE

`ten years of service as the Commissioner` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2036-03-01`
`two spells of service with a gap` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2030-03-01`, `a spell from 2032-06-01 to 2036-06-01`
`one spell of service that is already 12 years` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2038-03-01`
`a spell as a designated person` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2027-05-01 as a designated person`
`one spell of 1,461 days` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2030-03-01`

#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service that make up twelve years` `A` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS 4383
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service that make up twelve years` `B of F9.6` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS 4380
-- no prior service: 12 years from the start of the appointment
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `no service before` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 3 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.6` `no service before` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 2 26
-- trap T21: ten years served as the Commissioner (3,653 days), re-appointed from 1 March 2036 for 5 years: the 12 years are complete 730 days later, two years into the new term
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service in` `ten years of service as the Commissioner` EQUALS 3653
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `ten years of service as the Commissioner` (YMD 2036 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 3 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.6` `ten years of service as the Commissioner` (YMD 2036 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 2 26
-- the aggregate of two spells with a gap: 1,461 + 1,461 = 2,922 days served; from 1 January 2037 the remaining 1,461 days end on 1 January 2041 (B: 1,458 days, 29 December 2040)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service in` `two spells of service with a gap` EQUALS 2922
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `two spells of service with a gap` (YMD 2037 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2041 1 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.6` `two spells of service with a gap` (YMD 2037 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2040 12 29
-- 12 years already served: the cap is reached on the first day of the new appointment, whatever the reading
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `one spell of service that is already 12 years` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2040 1 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.6` `one spell of service that is already 12 years` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2040 1 1
-- the discriminating case of F9.6: 1,461 days served from 1 March 2026, then from 1 January 2031 the cap falls on 1 January 2039 under A (4,383 days in all) and on 29 December 2038 under B (4,380 days)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `one spell of 1,461 days` (YMD 2031 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2039 1 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.6` `one spell of 1,461 days` (YMD 2031 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 12 29
-- F9.11: 14 months as a designated relevant person (426 days) before an appointment from 1 June 2027. A: that service does not count, so 12 years from the appointment, 1 June 2039. B: it counts, so the cap falls 31 days after 1 March 2038, on 1 April 2038.
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `A` `a spell as a designated person` (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2039 6 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.11` `a spell as a designated person` (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 4 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service in` `a spell as a designated person` EQUALS 426
-- service as the Commissioner appointed counts under both readings of F9.11
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which twelve years of service are completed` `B of F9.11` `ten years of service as the Commissioner` (YMD 2036 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2038 3 1

§ `F9.7: not later than 4 months after the end of the year`
`B of F9.7` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.7 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a report on a calendar year` `A` 2026 4 EQUALS YMD 2027 4 30
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a report on a calendar year` `B of F9.7` 2026 4 EQUALS YMD 2027 5 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `A` 2026 (YMD 2027 4 30) 4
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `B of F9.7` 2026 (YMD 2027 4 30) 4
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `A` 2026 (YMD 2027 5 1) 4
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `B of F9.7` 2026 (YMD 2027 5 1) 4
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `A` 2026 (YMD 2027 5 2) 4
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report was provided within that many months after the end of the year` `B of F9.7` 2026 (YMD 2027 5 2) 4
-- another year: 2023
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the latest day for a report on a calendar year` `A` 2023 4 EQUALS YMD 2024 4 30

§ `F9.10: as soon as practicable`
`B of F9.10, 28 days` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.10 is read as B with 28 days`
-- reading A: the judgement is the input, whatever the days
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `A` TRUE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `A` FALSE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 2 2)
-- reading B: due 1 February 2027, 28 days allowed: taken 1 March is in time (28 days), 15 March is not (42 days); the judgement is ignored; a step before the due day is not a step after it
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `B of F9.10, 28 days` FALSE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `B of F9.10, 28 days` TRUE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `B of F9.10, 28 days` TRUE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `B of F9.10, 28 days` TRUE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 1 31)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a step was taken as soon as practicable` `B of F9.10, 28 days` FALSE (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 2 1)

§ `F9.12: a report for each calendar year`
`B of F9.12` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.12 is read as B`
-- the office held from 1 November 2026 to 30 June 2027
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2026
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2027
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2028
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `B of F9.12` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2026
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `B of F9.12` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2027
-- the office held throughout 2026 (1 June 2025 to 31 December 2027): both readings require a report for 2026; for 2025 and 2027 only A requires one if the year is partly held; 2027 is held whole
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) 2026
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `B of F9.12` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) 2026
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `A` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) 2025
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `B of F9.12` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) 2025
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: a report is required of the holder for a calendar year` `B of F9.12` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) 2027

§ `F9.9 text: the Dormant Bank Accounts words by vintage`
-- trap T22: the words are added by L.1/2017 from 16 December 2019 (the Table of Legislation History). The text of 1 January 2019 and of 31 May 2019 lacks them; every later text has them.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 1 January 2019`
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 1 January 2020`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 2 March 2021`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 12 April 2023`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 27 February 2024`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 16 October 2025`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026`

§ `The readings called directly (each reading of a fork is a function with its own test)`

§§ `F9.3: where the office ends`
-- notice given on 30 November 2026, the resignation naming 2 March 2027: the office ends on the day named (A, C) or on the day the notice is given (B)
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading A: the office ends when the notice period runs out` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 2
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading B: the office ends when the notice is given` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 11 30
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading C: the office ends when the notice period runs out, the months having been rolled` (YMD 2026 11 30) (YMD 2027 3 2) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 2
-- and the three readings of the earliest day, called directly: 30 November 2026 plus 3 months
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading A: the earliest day a resignation can take effect, the months being clamped` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading B: the earliest day a notice can be for, the office ending when the notice is given` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
#ASSERT `F9.3 reading C: the earliest day a resignation can take effect, the months being rolled` (YMD 2026 11 30) 3 EQUALS YMD 2027 3 2

§§ `F9.4, F9.5, F9.7, F9.14 and F9.1, F9.2: the reading functions`
-- called directly in the sections above (the functions named `F9.n reading A/B: ...` appear in those assertions)
#ASSERT `F9.4 reading A: the days of absence, both ends included, are longer than that many weeks` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 29) 4
#ASSERT NOT `F9.4 reading B: the elapsed days of absence are longer than that many weeks` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 29) 4
#ASSERT `F9.5 reading A: the latest day for a notice after an event is that many weeks after it` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `F9.5 reading B: the latest day for a notice after an event is the day before that many weeks after it` (YMD 2026 3 1) 2 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `F9.7 reading A: the latest day for a report on a calendar year, the months being clamped` 2026 4 EQUALS YMD 2027 4 30
#ASSERT `F9.7 reading B: the latest day for a report on a calendar year, the months being rolled` 2026 4 EQUALS YMD 2027 5 1
#ASSERT `F9.14 reading A: the latest day for the views to be sought is the day before the appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14
#ASSERT `F9.14 reading B: the latest day for the views to be sought is the day of the appointment` (YMD 2026 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `F9.2 reading A: the latest end date of a term is the anniversary of its start` (YMD 2026 3 1) 6 EQUALS YMD 2032 3 1
#ASSERT `F9.2 reading B: the latest end date of a term is the day before the anniversary of its start` (YMD 2026 3 1) 6 EQUALS YMD 2032 2 29

§§ `F9.6: the days that make up twelve years`
#ASSERT `F9.6 reading A: the days in twelve calendar years from the first day of service` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS 4383
#ASSERT `F9.6 reading B: the days in twelve years of 365 days` EQUALS 4380

§§ `F9.10: as soon as practicable, the two readings`
-- reading A: the judgement is the answer, whatever the days
#ASSERT `F9.10 reading A: a step is as soon as practicable when the person who decides finds it so` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `F9.10 reading A: a step is as soon as practicable when the person who decides finds it so` FALSE
-- reading B: due 1 February 2027, 28 days: 1 March is the 28th day (in time), 2 March the 29th (late), 31 January is before the step fell due
#ASSERT `F9.10 reading B: a step is as soon as practicable when it is taken within that many days of falling due` 28 (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `F9.10 reading B: a step is as soon as practicable when it is taken within that many days of falling due` 28 (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `F9.10 reading B: a step is as soon as practicable when it is taken within that many days of falling due` 28 (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 1 31)
-- the last day: reading A fixes none; reading B is the day it fell due plus the days
#ASSERT `F9.10 reading A: a judgement fixes no last day` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `F9.10 reading B: the last day is that many days after the day the step falls due` 28 (YMD 2027 2 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 1)
-- with the longer limit of 4 months in no case after: the earlier of 1 March 2027 and 30 April 2027
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable and in no case after a day` `B of F9.10, 28 days` (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 4 30) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable and in no case after a day` `A` (YMD 2027 2 1) (YMD 2027 4 30) EQUALS YMD 2027 4 30
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable` `A` (YMD 2027 2 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the last day for a step that is to be taken as soon as practicable` `B of F9.10, 28 days` (YMD 2027 2 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 3 1)

§§ `F9.11: whether service as a designated relevant person is counted`
`a designated spell and an ordinary spell` MEANS LIST `a spell from 2026-03-01 to 2027-05-01 as a designated person`, `a spell from 2032-06-01 to 2036-06-01`
#ASSERT count (`F9.11 reading A: service as a designated relevant person is left out` `a designated spell and an ordinary spell`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`F9.11 reading B: service as a designated relevant person is counted` `a designated spell and an ordinary spell`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service in` (`Sch 1 and 2: the periods of service that count toward twelve years` `A` `a designated spell and an ordinary spell`) EQUALS 1461
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the days of service in` (`Sch 1 and 2: the periods of service that count toward twelve years` `B of F9.11` `a designated spell and an ordinary spell`) EQUALS 1887

§§ `F9.12: a report for a year in which the office was held in part`
#ASSERT `F9.12 reading A: a report is required for a year in which the office was held on at least one day` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2026
#ASSERT NOT `F9.12 reading B: a report is required only for a year in which the office was held on every day` (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2027 6 30) 2026
#ASSERT `F9.12 reading B: a report is required only for a year in which the office was held on every day` (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2027 12 31) 2026

§§ `F9.17: a member of the States`
-- the person became a member on 15 June 2030, after the term began on 1 March 2026: both readings give that day
#ASSERT `F9.17 reading A: only becoming a member of the States during the appointment ends it` (YMD 2030 6 15) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2030 6 15)
#ASSERT `F9.17 reading B: being a member of the States at any time during the appointment ends it` (YMD 2030 6 15) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2030 6 15)
-- a member since 1 January 2025, before the term began: A finds no day, B the first day of the term
#ASSERT `F9.17 reading A: only becoming a member of the States during the appointment ends it` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `F9.17 reading B: being a member of the States at any time during the appointment ends it` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- becoming a member on the first day of the term itself is becoming a member during the appointment
#ASSERT `F9.17 reading A: only becoming a member of the States during the appointment ends it` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
`B of F9.17` MEANS `the favoured interpretation, but F9.17 is read as B`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which membership of the States ends the appointment` `A` NOTHING (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which membership of the States ends the appointment` `A` (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the day on which membership of the States ends the appointment` `B of F9.17` (JUST (YMD 2025 1 1)) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)

§§ `F9.19: the ground of absence`
-- (the Minister is satisfied, the absence is longer than the number of weeks)
#ASSERT `F9.19 reading A: the ground of absence needs the Minister's satisfaction and an absence of the length` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `F9.19 reading A: the ground of absence needs the Minister's satisfaction and an absence of the length` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `F9.19 reading A: the ground of absence needs the Minister's satisfaction and an absence of the length` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `F9.19 reading B: the ground of absence needs the Minister's satisfaction alone` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `F9.19 reading B: the ground of absence needs the Minister's satisfaction alone` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `F9.19 reading B: the ground of absence needs the Minister's satisfaction alone` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the ground of absence for terminating an appointment is made out` `A` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the ground of absence for terminating an appointment is made out` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.19 is read as B` TRUE FALSE
